ction regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reported as verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy, and v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Before the rollback, all regions were on v2.3.1 with an error rate of 0.18.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the follow-ups. It paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI haven't re-checked the error rate since the rollback. The follow-ups are to confirm it returns to baseline and to investigate the v2.3.1 failure before releasing again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PZ5xiwPwmwKdX58MRFU4VW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012sthBututn9K2mcvLpdLUr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. Both v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are unhealthy, and all three regions are currently on v2.3.1. Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PiQYfdGLzBsE4qnJnJpfHi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P8aHBjU4nCsiijrcDz9Nuc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate was 0.18, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Deployment history shows v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 both unhealthy; v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback reported VERIFIED. Follow-up: confirm error rate returns to baseline, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reported as verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy, and v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Before the rollback, all regions were on v2.3.1 with an error rate of 0.18.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the follow-ups. It paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI haven't re-checked the error rate since the rollback. The follow-ups are to confirm it returns to baseline and to investigate the v2.3.1 failure before releasing again.", "type": "text"}]}]}